    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW28jXjUaoq76mQCkZLcJxtaz)_\n\n## What\n\nRemoves `sp-minibuffer` and its `minibuffer-setup-hook` line from `sp-fonts` (#161), which remapped `default` and set `text-scale` in the minibuffer buffer on every prompt and mirrored the minibuffer / glitched `M-x` in `vertico-posframe`.\n\nThe larger text now comes from one setting: `sp-posframe-update-font` turns `sp-minibuffer-face` (fontaine, 1.36 of `default` in `regular`) into `vertico-posframe-font`, a font spec with the `default` family at that size. It runs once at load and on `fontaine-set-preset-hook`; nothing runs per prompt. This is step 2 of the rebuild plan in the `sp-posframe` doc.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- The size no longer follows `text-scale-adjust` of the calling buffer.\n- Prompts shown at the bottom of the frame (plain `read-string`, `y-or-n-p`) and the terminal fallback keep the `default` size.\n- If the glitch returns, set `vertico-posframe-font` to nil first (one line to bisect).\n\nDocs (`sp-fonts.org`, `sp-posframe.org`) and CHANGELOG updated. Not run in Emacs (none in the container); please check the posframe size with `M-x`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8ooNzim25iTWhixoA)_",
